window.products.push({"id":1067495,"name":"Rainbow Store QCC1 Regulator Valve Propane Refill Adapter for All 1 LB Tank Small Cylinders - 100% Solid Brass Valve with Safety Protection","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71WCXghWuOL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","description":"Brass Propane Refill Adapter Lp Gas Cylinder Tank 0.35 pounds small attachment coupler It's that time of year again! Time to go on a camping trip! Unfortunately, you need to refill those propane bottles again to make your delicious summertime fare! It gets quite expensive after a while. Well it's time to start saving. Introducing the Brass Propane Refill Adapter, a handy tool you can use to fill up your propane bottles for less! Simply attach the adaptor to your propane tank and you can fill your propane bottles yourself instead of throwing out and buying new bottles. Save money, save the environment, get yours today!Package Includes: 1 x QCC1 Regulator Valve Propane Refill AdapterQuick Instruction:Step 1. Shut valve to BBQ propane tank.Step 2. Insert nose tip of the adapter into a 20 to 50 lbs BBQ propane tank fill connection.Step 3. Turn the adapter handheel grip clockwise to a tight fit.Step 4. Screw in the 1 lb cylinder propane tank clockwise into the adapter.Step 5. Turn BBQ tank upside down then open BBQ tank valve.Step 6. You will begin to hear the propane gas transferring into the 1 lb cylinder tank.Step 7. The regulator valve in the adapter will automatically cut off the flow of gas when a certain pressure is reached to avoid overfilling so sit back and allow it to fill on its own.Step 8. When no more sound is coming from the tank, simply shut the BBQ valve and remove the 1 lb propane cylinder tank.Pay attention to:1. You need to turn your bulk tank upside down so liquid flows out of it.2. You need to chill your empty tanks so that there is a lower vapor pressure in the empty tank than the bulk tank.3. Your refilled tanks will not be totally full, but this is good because over filling can cause them to vent gas if left in a hot place.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71WCXghWuOL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Rainbow Store","source_asin":"B07JG2LRV1","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-1067495","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07JG2LRV1","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B07JG2LRV1","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
